:Connected));","+    }","     EXPECT_CALL(client_connection_callbacks, onEvent(Network::ConnectionEvent::RemoteClose))","         .WillOnce(Invoke([&](Network::ConnectionEvent) -> void { close_second_time(); }));","     EXPECT_CALL(server_connection_callbacks, onEvent(Network::ConnectionEvent::RemoteClose))","@@ -1315,7 +1390,14 @@ void testUtilV2(const TestUtilOptionsV2& options) {","   }"," ","   if (!options.expectedClientStats().empty()) {","-    EXPECT_EQ(1UL, client_stats_store.counter(options.expectedClientStats()).value());","+    // When the client's handshake completes before the server rejects it, closing the socket calls","+    // SSL_shutdown(). OpenSSL fails that call after the fatal alert, counting a second error.","+    const uint64_t expected_client_count =","+        !options.expectSuccess() && options.expectClientConnectedBeforeFailure()","+            ? SSL_SELECT(1UL, 2UL)","+            : 1UL;","+    EXPECT_EQ(expected_client_count,","+              client_stats_store.counter(options.expectedClientStats()).value());","   }"," ","   if (options.expectSuccess()) {","@@ -1330,6 +1412,14 @@ void testUtilV2(const TestUtilOptionsV2& options) {","   }"," }"," ","+// Runs testUtilV2() for a server that rejects the client certificate, once with TLS 1.2 and once","+// with TLS 1.3. With TLS 1.3, the client completes its handshake before the server validates the","+// client certificate, so the client sees Connected before the server closes the connection.","+void testUtilV2ClientCertRejected(TestUtilOptionsV2& options) {","+  testUtilV2(options.setClientTlsVersion(TlsParameters::TLSv1_2));","+  testUtilV2(options.setClientTlsVersion(TlsParameters::TLSv1_3));","+}","+"," void updateFilterChain(","     const envoy::extensions::transport_sockets::tls::v3::DownstreamTlsContext& tls_context,","     envoy::config::listener::v3::FilterChain& filter_chain) {","@@ -3460,7 +3550,7 @@ TEST_P(SslSocketTest, NoCertUntrustedNotPermitted) {"," )EOF\";"," ","   TestUtil